"""Independent open-book application questions; indices intentionally balanced."""
QUESTIONS=[]
def q(stem,options,answer,feedback):QUESTIONS.append(dict(question=stem,options=options,answer=answer,feedback=feedback))
q('A team verified the installed vessel against its accepted arrangement. Which conclusion is supported?', ['Every future batch will meet its mixing specification','The installed arrangement matches the reviewed scope','The cleaning process removes all relevant residues'],1,'Limit the conclusion to installation evidence; performance and cleaning need their own studies.')
q('Two inspectors used different revisions of the instrument schedule. What should happen?', ['Reconcile baseline revisions and assess affected checks','Combine both checklists without evaluating the differences','Use the newest issue without checking its effective approval'],0,'A consistent applicable baseline is needed to interpret the observations.')
q('An equipment tag matches but the manufacturer serial differs from the schedule. What is justified?', ['Accept the vessel because the site tag is the primary identifier','Replace the schedule entry without investigating the difference','Resolve the identity discrepancy before relying on the match'],2,'A tag match does not resolve conflicting equipment identity.')
q('A drawing lacks the required removal clearance. How should a measured 300 mm be treated?', ['As a universal GMP minimum for maintenance access','As an observation whose acceptance criterion remains unresolved','As proof that the manufacturer removal envelope is satisfied'],1,'The observed distance cannot create its own criterion; no universal 300 mm limit is taught.')
q('A gasket certificate describes a lot that cannot be linked to the installed gasket. How should it be handled?', ['Resolve the installed-gasket link before accepting the certificate','Accept the certificate because supplier and material grade match','Accept the gasket because the vessel-body certificate is available'],0,'The missing item-to-evidence link must be resolved through an applicable controlled approach.')
q('The installed material matches its specification. Which claim still needs separate evidence?', ['The compared material identifier matches the specification','The identity record relates to the inspected component','The cleaning process is effective for the intended residues'],2,'Matching material identity does not demonstrate cleaning effectiveness.')
q('A utility line is labelled correctly but connected to a different branch than the drawing specifies. What is appropriate?', ['Accept the label as sufficient evidence of correct installation','Record and investigate the connection discrepancy','Revise the drawing to match without an impact assessment'],1,'A label does not correct an incorrect or unassessed physical connection.')
q('A utility was qualified before a new vessel branch was added. What is needed for the extension?', ['Assessment of the change and applicable verification scope','Automatic acceptance under the original utility report','Confirm source quality and omit branch-specific installation checks'],0,'The extension must be evaluated; previous qualification does not automatically cover a changed system.')
q('Indication is 40.4 °C and reference is 40.0 °C. Which signed error and simple comparison are correct?', ['−0.4 °C; outside the fictional ±0.5 °C limit','+0.8 °C; outside the fictional ±0.5 °C limit','+0.4 °C; within the fictional ±0.5 °C limit'],2,'Indication minus reference is +0.4 °C. This arithmetic is not a complete uncertainty or acceptance decision.')
q('A current certificate has suitable range but identifies another instrument. What follows?', ['Use it because the range covers the planned test','Resolve certificate applicability to the installed instrument','Use it because both instruments came from one supplier'],1,'Identity, not just date and range, is necessary for applicability.')
q('An instrument is found outside its required calibration status after IQ measurements. What should be assessed?', ['Whether a new calibration alone can replace the affected readings','Whether the signed observations can be accepted without impact review','The validity of affected measurements and required follow-up'],2,'A new calibration record alone does not establish the validity of earlier evidence.')
q('The control-system version is recorded during IQ. Which next step is still needed as applicable?', ['Validation of applicable functions and controls under the plan','Acceptance of all audit-trail behaviour from the version number','Acceptance of backup restoration from the version screenshot'],0,'Version identification does not demonstrate functional controls or complete Annex 11 compliance.')
q('A supplier manual covers a different installed model. What is the strongest response?', ['File it because the product family is broadly similar','Verify applicability and obtain the required correct instructions','Use the similar model instructions pending the next periodic review'],1,'The handover needs instructions relevant to the installed model/configuration.')
q('A factory test is proposed for reuse after transport and site assembly. What supports reuse?', ['An approved factory report without reviewing site configuration','Matching model numbers without assessing transport or assembly','Applicable evidence plus justified configuration and impact review'],2,'Assess configuration, method, data and effects of transport/installation; retain required site checks.')
q('A photograph shows a readable nameplate but cannot be linked to any location or check. What is needed?', ['Link the image to the inspected item and its verification record','Placement in the general vessel folder without a check reference','Use as sole identity evidence for every unit of the same model'],0,'An image needs a clear relationship to the relevant equipment and verification record.')
q('A serial number was transposed in a handwritten record. Which correction is appropriate?', ['Erase the entry and write the expected serial in its place','Preserve the original and make an attributed, dated correction','Rewrite the page and discard the page with the original entry'],1,'Follow the approved procedure, preserve the original information and record a reason where appropriate.')
q('A protocol check was not performed because access was unsafe. Which status is accurate?', ['Passed because the remaining equipment was satisfactory','Not applicable because inspection was inconvenient','Not checked, with the limitation and follow-up recorded'],2,'An incomplete check is distinct from a justified scope exclusion or a demonstrated pass.')
q('An installed valve differs from the accepted specification. Which route is defensible?', ['Record the finding, assess impact and authorize the response','Edit the acceptance criterion to match the supplied valve','Close the check when the supplier confirms receipt of the complaint'],0,'A discrepancy requires an evidence-based controlled response and defined verification.')
q('Nine of ten checks are supported, but gasket traceability remains open. What does 90% mean?', ['Numerical coverage only; it does not authorize the next stage','Automatic OQ permission because it exceeds the practice target','Complete installation suitability if the missing record is promised'],0,'9/10 is 90%, but significance and activity-specific assessment govern the decision.')
q('A proposed dry OQ activity is unaffected by an open wetted-system finding. What supports conditional progression?', ['The project schedule and the supplier commitment to close the finding','The number of completed checks and the overall practice score','Documented no-significant-impact review and responsible authorization'],2,'Annex 15 §2.10 addresses conditional approval to proceed to the next qualification stage after a documented no-significant-impact assessment. Selecting a separately assessed dry OQ activity is a practical teaching recommendation, not an activity prescribed by that clause. The open finding remains open; responsible authorization is required.')

# Fixed irregular order makes the reviewed key reproducible; it is not a runtime shuffle.
POSITIONS=[2,0,0,1,2,1,0,2,1,1,2,0,2,0,1,2,0,1,2,0]
for item,position in zip(QUESTIONS,POSITIONS):
 correct=item['options'][item['answer']]
 others=[option for n,option in enumerate(item['options']) if n!=item['answer']]
 others.insert(position,correct);item['options']=others;item['answer']=position
